<p>The <strong class="selflink">CLA_ 2da</strong> defines the available Player and NPC <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Class" title="Class (page does not exist)">classes</a> and <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Specialization" title="Specialization (page does not exist)">specializations</a>.
</p><p>This <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/2DA" title="2da">2da</a> is defined as an <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/M2da" title="M2da (page does not exist)">m2da</a> in the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/M2DA%20base%202da" title="M2DA base 2da">M2DA_base 2da</a> and has an <b>ID</b> of 3. It can be extended by m2da fragments which have names starting with <b>CLA_</b>. It can be referenced in scripting using the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/TABLE" title="TABLE *">TABLE_RULES_CLASSES</a> constant defined in <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/2da%20constants%20h" title="2da constants h">2da_constants_h</a>. 
</p>
